                <head>No. 330.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Anderson to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Copenhagen</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-12-16"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 16, 1887</date>.
                        (Received January 3, 1888.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 184.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that John A.
                    Benson’s brother who traveled with him under the assumed name of William B.
                    Frank, and in regard to whom you telegraphed me that there was no indictment
                    against him, will be released from prison in Copenhagen on Wednesday, December
                    21, and will sail on that day in a Thingvalla steamer direct for New York.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">R. B.
                            Anderson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
